    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d622">

                <pb facs="0699" n="687" sameAs="frus:frus1944v03/pg687"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851.01/3805: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Hamilton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-05-17T09:00:00+03:00">May 17, 1944—9
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 6:42 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1754. See Embassy’s 1666, May 12, 10 a.m. and previous.<anchor n="86"
                        xml:id="d622-f1"/> The following is a paraphrased translation of a note from
                    Molotov dated May 16.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“The Soviet Government, having studied the draft directive<anchor n="87"
                            xml:id="d622-f2"/> to General Eisenhower in the event of the occupation
                        of French territory contained in your letters of April 11 and May 10, has
                        reached the conclusion that the requirements of the military situation which
                        will <pb facs="0700" n="688" xml:id="pg688"/> be created as the result of an
                        invasion of the territory of France by Allied forces are met by this
                        directive.</p>
                    <p>I shall be grateful if you will transmit the above to the United States
                        Government.”</p>
                </quote>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hamilton</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
